  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider the function $y=\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}.$ The derivative of this function is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x-1}}{(1-3x)^{6}}g(x)+\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$",
